- Tax is rounded *up* to the minor unit. That is what tax authorities require, and what naive
- rounding gets wrong in exactly the cases which matter. Twenty per cent of £2.94 is £0.588,
- which is charged as £0.59:
+ El impuesto se redondea *hacia arriba* a la unidad menor. Es lo que exigen las administraciones
+ tributarias, y lo que el redondeo ingenuo hace mal precisamente en los casos que importan. El
+ veinte por ciento de 2,94 £ es 0,588 £, que se cobra como 0,59 £:

= which is charged as £0.59:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= which is charged as £0.59:
